{"type":"assistant","uuid":"a7e83eca-2832-46ed-8f0c-e8380a6a058c","session_id":"31fd3a90-bf72-4f98-bd2c-5539a42c8020","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"a7e83eca-2832-46ed-8f0c-e8380a6a058c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fix is correctly applied. Let me now provide a summary and the final patch output.\n\nThe bug was:\n- Filters don't work if the title contains the word \"brain\"\n- Filters don't work in \"top 24\" and \"48\" views\n\nRoot cause:\n- The `loadAlgolia()` method, which handles \"Top 24 hours\", \"Top 48 hours\", and \"Top 7 days\" views (via Algolia API), was missing the filter logic that exists in `loadStory()` method.\n- `loadStory()` checks `filterWords` and `filterDomains` to filter out stories matching filter phrases.\n- `loadAlgolia()` only filtered out clicked stories but never applied word/domain filters.\n\nThe fix:\n- Added the same filtering logic to `loadAlgolia()` that exists in `loadStory()`:\n  1. Filter stories by title containing filter words (case-insensitive)\n  2. Filter stories by URL containing filter domains (case-insensitive)\n  3. Uses `Utils.getFilterWords()` and `Utils.getFilterDomains()` to get the filter lists\n\nLet me present the final output.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"214a6b56-4c93-4dfd-a1fd-c24eb1f75afe","session_id":"31fd3a90-bf72-4f98-bd2c-5539a42c8020","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"214a6b56-4c93-4dfd-a1fd-c24eb1f75afe","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe fix is correctly applied. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root Cause:** The `loadAlgolia()` method in `StoriesFragment.java` was missing filter logic for `filterWords` and `filterDomains`. \n\n**Why it happened:** The app uses two different code paths for loading stories:\n1. **`loadStory()`** — used for normal HN API views (Ask, Show, Jobs). This method checks `filterWords` and `filterDomains` after loading each story.\n2. **`loadAlgolia()`** — used for Algolia-backed views (Top 24h, Top 48h, Top 7d). This method was missing the filter checks entirely, only filtering out already-clicked stories.\n\nWhen the user set \"brain\" as a filter word, stories with \"brain\" in the title were correctly filtered in normal views (via `loadStory()`), but not in Top 24/48 views (via `loadAlgolia()`).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nAdded filtering logic to `loadAlgolia()` in `StoriesFragment.java` (lines 742-765):\n\n```java\n// Filter by filter words and filter domains\nArrayList<String> words = Utils.getFilterWords(getContext());\nArrayList<String> domains = Utils.getFilterDomains(getContext());\nIterator<Story> filterIterator = stories.iterator();\nwhile (filterIterator.hasNext()) {\n    Story story = filterIterator.next();\n    boolean shouldFilter = false;\n    for (String phrase : words) {\n        if (story.title.toLowerCase().contains(phrase.toLowerCase())) {\n            shouldFilter = true;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    if (!shouldFilter && story.url != null) {\n        for (String phrase : domains) {\n            if (story.url.toLowerCase().contains(phrase.toLowerCase())) {\n                shouldFilter = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    if (shouldFilter) {\n        filterIterator.remove();\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis mirrors the exact same filtering logic already present in `loadStory()`, ensuring consistency across all views. The filtering is case-insensitive and applies to both story titles (word filters) and story URLs (domain filters)."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50859,"output_tokens":729,"cache_read_input_tokens":48208,"total_tokens":51588}}}
